<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Asmara</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Asmara is the capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrea">Eritrea</a>, on the highland plateau at about 2,300 metres. A village grew into a city after the Italians made it the capital of their colony in the 1890s, and in the 1930s it was rebuilt with modernist and Art Deco buildings. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eritrean-war-of-independence">Eritrean War of Independence</a> it was an Ethiopian stronghold until 1991. Its centre is a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/asmara.jpg" alt="Asmara" width="320" height="411" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Tigernssnowy7 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Asmara_Montage.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
